# Repository documentation

These files are read by contributors and agents working in *this* repo. The root
`AGENTS.md` is the only one loaded on every turn, so it is the expensive one.

Budgets, enforced by `modTestRepoDocs`:

- Root `AGENTS.md` — **150 lines**. It is a router, not a manual.
- Each `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` — **120 lines**.
- Every `docs/*.md` must be reachable from the root `AGENTS.md` routing table,
  from a rule, or from the `docs/README.md` index. Orphaned docs fail the test.
- Every `docs/` link in the root `AGENTS.md` must resolve to a real file.

Before adding to any of them, read
[docs/agent-docs-maintenance.md](../../docs/agent-docs-maintenance.md), which has
the gate for whether the content belongs in agent documentation at all and the
routing table for which file it goes in.

Two rules do most of the work:

- **Anything recoverable by listing a folder or opening one source file does not
  belong in the always-loaded set.** Class inventories, folder trees, and enum
  members drift and cost tokens on every turn.
- **New depth goes in `docs/`, not in `AGENTS.md`.** Add a routing-table row
  pointing at it and a row to the `docs/README.md` index.

`Version Control.accda.src/AGENTS.md` and `vcs-agent-docs/` are a different
audience with stricter rules; see
[agent-docs.mdc](agent-docs.mdc).
